STREAM NOT CAPTURED.

The Stage A run was executed through an orchestration layer that did not tee this stream to a
file, and the stream is not recoverable after the fact. This file records that absence rather
than reconstructing content that was never saved: fabricating a log would be a violation of
AGENTS.md rule 9, and a reconstructed log is worse than a missing one because it looks complete.

What IS preserved, and is sufficient to recompute every reported number:
  - raw-result.json      full machine-readable per-gate results (the run's actual output)
  - command.txt          the exact command, re-runnable
  - environment.json     interpreter, platform, dependency versions, cpu count
  - manifest.yaml        seeds, per-phase timings, git commit and dirty state, validity status
  - ../../../../coordination/goals/GOAL-HQC-001/batches/BATCH-6fddee/tasks/TASK-20260806-64b506/
                         stage_a.py (the runner itself) and stage_a_report.md

The independent validator recomputed the four artifact hashes and ~40 numbers from raw-result.json
without needing this stream. Future runs under this experiment MUST tee stdout and stderr.
